{"name":"Chicken Masala","hex":"#cc8822","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chicken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domesticated subspecies of red junglefowl (Gallus gallus domesticus).","The meat from this bird eaten as food."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cowardly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken"},{"term":"masala","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many blends of spices used in Indian cuisine, most often containing cardamom, coriander, mace together with pepper, nutmeg, fennel seeds, jeera etc.","Any dish prepared with such spices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masala"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chicken tikka masala","blocks":[{"text":"Chicken tikka masala is a curry consisting of roasted marinated chicken pieces in a creamy spiced sauce (masala). It is thought to have been created in Britain, possibly by Ali Ahmed Aslam in Glasgow. It is offered at restaurants around the world and in some of its forms is similar to butter chicken."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Chicken_tikka_masala_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Chicken_tikka_masala_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken_tikka_masala"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https